--
N5008 [expr.delete]/3, [class.dtor]/13: deleting a D through a pointer to
either of its A subobjects calls D's destructor, which destroys both A
subobjects; C::id is the final overrider in C's A only ([class.virtual]/2).
The front end rejected the class.  g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept this
program, and it fails only its WRONG assertion.
